From 29a93d814882ce07df9057883e0e533a544db987 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 15:27:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32: remove CRC node from stm32mp1x device trees

CRC drivers has been dropped in kernel v6.17 [1], remove support from
stm32mp151.dtsi and stm32mp131.dtsi.
Also remove activation from all boards.

[1]: 5b019bb25fbf ("crypto: stm32 - remove crc32 and crc32c support")

Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I59d30f95b3a9f14a5c04d21db55817abcb27752b
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/612834
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
